WEBVTT

00:00:25.670 --> 00:00:28.970
Gobble!! Guts!! Gobble!! Guts!! Gobble!!

00:00:30.810 --> 00:00:34.210
Gobble!! Guts!! Gobble!! Guts!! Gobble!!

00:00:36.410 --> 00:00:39.050
Calling everything delicious!

00:00:39.050 --> 00:00:43.550
The more I eat, the more powerful I get!

00:00:44.120 --> 00:00:46.920
Let’s capture ingredients around the world!

00:00:46.920 --> 00:00:51.500
I dream of being an invincible 
Gourmet Fighter!!

00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:56.530
Now on to the bottom of the 
sea, or the tops of glaciers!

00:00:56.530 --> 00:00:59.200
Jump! Jump Jump Jump! 
Knock! Knock Knock Knock!

00:00:59.200 --> 00:01:01.400
Give thanks!

00:01:01.400 --> 00:01:04.610
Let’s eat!

00:01:05.040 --> 00:01:10.410
Wow wo!! Spiked Punch! Wow wo!! Multi-fold!

00:01:10.410 --> 00:01:15.550
Guts! Gutsy Guts! I can eat any dream!

00:01:15.550 --> 00:01:20.820
Wow wo!! My very own... 
Wow wo!! ...Full Course!

00:01:21.090 --> 00:01:24.990
Guts! Gutsy Guts! Gather them all up!

00:01:24.990 --> 00:01:31.070
And put the world on my plate!

00:01:31.070 --> 00:01:33.870
Wow wow wow! Eat the mountains!!

00:01:33.870 --> 00:01:36.440
Wow wow wow! Toriko!!

00:01:36.440 --> 00:01:39.040
Wow wow wow! Eat the oceans!!

00:01:39.040 --> 00:01:43.310
Wow wow wow! Tori, Tori, Tori, Toriko!!

00:01:52.350 --> 00:01:55.290
Someone once said...

00:01:56.790 --> 00:01:59.230
There are keyaki trees

00:01:59.230 --> 00:02:03.400
with leaves that have a pronounced 
flavor of ginger-fried pork...

00:02:05.200 --> 00:02:09.440
Ginger-fried Poryaki!

00:02:11.240 --> 00:02:15.440
There are sea urchins stuffed 
with sweet brownies...

00:02:15.440 --> 00:02:19.510
Sea Browchin!

00:02:21.250 --> 00:02:24.550
The world is in the Gourmet Age...

00:02:24.550 --> 00:02:29.520
An age in which people quest for 
yet unknown culinary delights!

00:02:31.690 --> 00:02:34.290
There are four more training 
ingredients that Ichiryu,

00:02:34.290 --> 00:02:37.060
the president of IGO, asked Toriko to get.

00:02:37.430 --> 00:02:40.400
In order to capture the Shining Gourami,

00:02:40.400 --> 00:02:44.300
Toriko and company headed for a cavern 
inside Death Falls in the Mors Mountains.

00:02:49.610 --> 00:02:53.210
Toriko and Sunny's combined 
attack deflected a mountain

00:02:53.210 --> 00:02:56.920
and they successfully entered the cavern 
where the Shining Gourami dwell. But...

00:02:57.750 --> 00:03:00.890
What I did exhausted me. I don't 
have any strength left either...

00:03:00.890 --> 00:03:03.060
Ain't there somethin' to eat around here?

00:03:03.060 --> 00:03:05.420
The two of us are gonna be useless 
'til we get somethin' in our bellies.

00:03:06.390 --> 00:03:09.330
Toriko and Sunny used up 
all of their strength.

00:03:09.660 --> 00:03:12.260
There is food! And it's first-rate!

00:03:12.500 --> 00:03:14.100
Shining Gourami!

00:03:14.800 --> 00:03:18.870
Komatsu advanced through the cavern alone 
in order to capture a Shining Gourami

00:03:18.870 --> 00:03:21.470
and arrived at a pond where they live.

00:03:21.940 --> 00:03:25.680
But he failed to capture one alive...

00:03:26.710 --> 00:03:30.650
In the end, will Komatsu be able 
to catch a Shining Gourami?

00:03:34.150 --> 00:03:38.420
Cooking by Intuition! Komatsu 
and the Shining Gourami!

00:03:47.400 --> 00:03:48.630
Just by touching it...

00:03:51.540 --> 00:03:53.300
I don't even think it's edible anymore!

00:03:54.370 --> 00:03:56.540
It's just like with the Puffer Whale...

00:03:57.040 --> 00:03:59.780
The Shining Gourami is a Special 
Preparation Ingredient.

00:04:00.210 --> 00:04:01.480
In which case...

00:04:06.050 --> 00:04:07.750
...I have to proceed cautiously.

00:04:10.190 --> 00:04:11.590
Cautiously...

00:04:14.190 --> 00:04:15.160
Here comes one!

00:04:15.160 --> 00:04:18.430
Quietly... so as not to excite it...

00:04:21.060 --> 00:04:22.430
Cautiously...

00:04:24.900 --> 00:04:26.600
Shoot!

00:04:26.600 --> 00:04:31.270
Cautiously... then match my movements 
with the Shining Gourami's...

00:04:37.550 --> 00:04:38.550
Now!

00:04:39.150 --> 00:04:40.180
Yes!

00:04:42.380 --> 00:04:43.550
Wow!

00:04:48.820 --> 00:04:52.390
Gently... carefully...

00:04:55.730 --> 00:04:57.100
Oh, no!

00:05:03.670 --> 00:05:05.270
No...

00:05:06.770 --> 00:05:09.740
We should've eaten that Potato Eel...

00:05:11.450 --> 00:05:15.880
We might've been able to join the 
hunt for the Shining Gourami then.

00:05:15.880 --> 00:05:17.720
I already told you!

00:05:17.720 --> 00:05:20.350
I know, I know. Your instinct...

00:05:20.350 --> 00:05:21.620
I'm starving!

00:05:34.700 --> 00:05:36.070
Again...

00:05:36.440 --> 00:05:39.340
Even though Toriko-san and 
Sunny-san are waiting...

00:05:41.840 --> 00:05:43.740
What should I do?!

00:05:45.110 --> 00:05:46.310
What should I do...?

00:05:48.580 --> 00:05:49.880
What should I do?

00:06:05.330 --> 00:06:06.270
Oil?

00:06:10.040 --> 00:06:14.370
I was so focused on the Shining 
Gourami that I didn't notice it...

00:06:15.910 --> 00:06:18.210
...but even with the suit on, I can tell.

00:06:18.210 --> 00:06:21.210
Smooth, thick water...

00:06:26.590 --> 00:06:30.220
Not exactly water, but... oil!

00:06:33.390 --> 00:06:34.730
What is this?!

00:06:40.730 --> 00:06:44.440
Even though their color changed when 
I barely touched them before...

00:07:00.180 --> 00:07:01.090
What's this?!

00:07:05.320 --> 00:07:06.390
Hey, Toriko...

00:07:07.020 --> 00:07:10.460
Before, you said you had no choice 
but to have faith in Matsu.

00:07:10.460 --> 00:07:12.630
But do we even have a way out of here?

00:07:14.130 --> 00:07:16.900
After all, the entrance is sealed up by 
the crumbled pieces of that mountain.

00:07:16.900 --> 00:07:19.000
What are we gonna do when it's time to go?

00:07:19.000 --> 00:07:20.640
No idea...

00:07:20.640 --> 00:07:23.240
I guess we'll just have to break 
it up again into smaller pieces.

00:07:23.240 --> 00:07:25.940
Can you do that when you're this hungry?

00:07:25.940 --> 00:07:27.140
Good point...

00:07:27.140 --> 00:07:29.410
And the instant we smash our way through,

00:07:29.410 --> 00:07:32.480
we'll get hit with several hundred million 
tons of water from the falls again.

00:07:34.350 --> 00:07:36.750
At any rate, Matsu is taking long.

00:07:37.290 --> 00:07:40.960
Toriko-san! Sunny-san!

00:07:39.460 --> 00:07:41.420
Something probably happened to him.

00:07:41.790 --> 00:07:45.730
Toriko-san! Sunny-san!

00:07:43.290 --> 00:07:47.560
Yeah, somethin' happened. Somethin' good!

00:07:49.100 --> 00:07:53.100
Toriko-san! Sunny-san!

00:07:53.470 --> 00:07:55.370
It's Matsu! That's definitely Matsu!

00:07:55.370 --> 00:07:57.670
Toriko-san! Sunny-san!

00:07:57.670 --> 00:08:02.080
Sorry to keep you waiting! I 
captured the Shining Gourami!

00:08:02.780 --> 00:08:03.980
Komatsu!

00:08:04.210 --> 00:08:06.150
Seriously?! Well done!

00:08:08.950 --> 00:08:10.750
So these are Shining Gourami!

00:08:10.750 --> 00:08:11.550
That's right!

00:08:10.920 --> 00:08:12.650
What amazing luminescence!

00:08:12.420 --> 00:08:14.520
Is this... Knocking?!

00:08:14.520 --> 00:08:17.930
Toriko-san, Sunny-san, 
let's hurry back and eat!

00:08:18.560 --> 00:08:21.430
The problem is, how do we get out of here?!

00:08:21.430 --> 00:08:23.430
Oh, that's right.

00:08:23.430 --> 00:08:25.070
You say we can't get out?

00:08:26.900 --> 00:08:30.040
Look. The exit is blocked by boulders.

00:08:30.040 --> 00:08:31.170
Oh, no!

00:08:31.810 --> 00:08:33.980
Can't we do something?!

00:08:36.210 --> 00:08:36.980
Queen!

00:08:36.980 --> 00:08:38.280
How did it get in here?!

00:08:42.280 --> 00:08:43.650
From the cracks between the rocks!

00:08:44.850 --> 00:08:48.220
I see! She slithered between the 
cracks of the crushed mountain!

00:08:50.060 --> 00:08:53.390
My guess is the mountain is holding 
the force of the water in check.

00:08:53.790 --> 00:08:56.930
We can get out by riding 
inside Queen's mouth!

00:09:00.970 --> 00:09:03.500
Alright! Let's get back fast!

00:09:03.500 --> 00:09:06.070
I wanna dine on Shining Gourami!

00:09:22.590 --> 00:09:23.960
Good job, Queen!

00:09:23.960 --> 00:09:27.730
That's right. Thanks to 
Queen-chan, we're saved.

00:09:28.060 --> 00:09:29.260
Thanks!

00:09:32.000 --> 00:09:35.170
Alright, let's get down to 
eating these Shining Gourami!

00:09:35.170 --> 00:09:36.140
Right!

00:09:41.640 --> 00:09:44.140
They glow so brightly, 
yet it's not blinding...

00:09:44.810 --> 00:09:47.410
It's like a gentle sunrise!

00:09:47.410 --> 00:09:49.280
What a beautiful fish...

00:09:49.710 --> 00:09:54.420
But even though it's glowing like 
this, it's cool to the touch.

00:09:54.420 --> 00:09:58.360
That's because the glow that creatures 
give off produce hardly any heat.

00:09:58.890 --> 00:10:02.790
That's why it's called "cold light".

00:10:02.790 --> 00:10:04.530
It's the same glow that fireflies have.

00:10:05.630 --> 00:10:09.230
And since Knocking has been used on 
them, they're maintaining their glow.

00:10:09.770 --> 00:10:11.640
But how did you do Knocking?

00:10:11.640 --> 00:10:14.940
Knocking? Uh, I just...

00:10:14.940 --> 00:10:19.040
Somehow, I managed to attract 
the Shining Gourami in the pond.

00:10:19.040 --> 00:10:23.680
When I pet the Shining Gourami near the 
surface of the translucent pond water,

00:10:23.680 --> 00:10:26.780
I felt like I could capture 
them for some reason,

00:10:26.780 --> 00:10:28.720
and it worked better than I imagined!

00:10:29.450 --> 00:10:31.890
It's said that if you put a frog 
on its back and pet its stomach,

00:10:31.890 --> 00:10:33.460
it'll become quiet,

00:10:33.720 --> 00:10:37.760
and the same kind of effect may 
apply to Shining Gourami, too.

00:10:37.760 --> 00:10:39.460
In this water?

00:10:39.260 --> 00:10:42.600
It seems like it's comfortable 
for the Shining Gourami.

00:10:44.100 --> 00:10:48.100
This water is really smooth... 
In fact, it's not water, but oil!

00:10:48.100 --> 00:10:49.110
That's right.

00:10:49.670 --> 00:10:53.610
It kind of smells like oleic acid... 
Like unsaturated fatty acid...

00:10:53.610 --> 00:10:55.750
As if it's high-grade olive oil...

00:10:57.150 --> 00:11:00.120
The Mors Mountains are 
over 15,000 meters high.

00:11:01.620 --> 00:11:04.850
The nutrients from those mountains 
collects in that pond.

00:11:05.890 --> 00:11:07.320
An oil-like substance

00:11:07.320 --> 00:11:10.390
extracted little by little from the 
flora and fauna of the mountains

00:11:10.390 --> 00:11:12.590
may be floating at the top of the pond.

00:11:13.330 --> 00:11:17.030
The Shining Gourami must 
like that oily top layer.

00:11:17.030 --> 00:11:18.430
I see...

00:11:18.430 --> 00:11:20.770
And swimming in unusual oil like that

00:11:20.770 --> 00:11:24.070
lessened the Shining Gourami's stress, huh?

00:11:24.070 --> 00:11:27.310
That's why I got lucky 
with my sort-of Knocking.

00:11:27.310 --> 00:11:29.040
It wasn't luck, Komatsu.

00:11:30.210 --> 00:11:33.880
You heard the voice of the 
ingredients, the Shining Gourami.

00:11:34.380 --> 00:11:36.050
That's your ability.

00:11:36.050 --> 00:11:39.950
Y-Yeah, but I failed with 
the first three fish.

00:11:39.950 --> 00:11:42.890
I barely touched them, 
but their color changed.

00:11:42.890 --> 00:11:48.300
I brought those three fish out too 
so IGO can investigate, but maybe...

00:11:48.300 --> 00:11:50.000
They're Special Preparation Ingredients?

00:11:50.000 --> 00:11:50.660
Yes.

00:11:50.660 --> 00:11:52.600
Just by touching them?

00:11:52.600 --> 00:11:54.500
I'd like to eat 'em as sashimi,

00:11:54.500 --> 00:11:57.300
but one wrong move with the 
knife and it's over, yeah?

00:11:57.300 --> 00:11:58.410
Right...

00:11:58.410 --> 00:12:00.240
Then how are you going to prepare them?

00:12:00.710 --> 00:12:04.510
Actually, I had an idea. I think 
I'll try frying them lightly.

00:12:04.510 --> 00:12:05.880
Tempura?!

00:12:06.110 --> 00:12:07.210
What do you think?

00:12:07.210 --> 00:12:09.650
Komatsu, you're gonna use that oil as it is?!

00:12:09.650 --> 00:12:10.220
Yes!

00:12:10.220 --> 00:12:13.050
The Shining Gourami are 
comfortable in this oil,

00:12:13.050 --> 00:12:15.060
so even if I suddenly fry them 
in it, maybe it'll be okay...

00:12:15.060 --> 00:12:19.160
Certainly, it's so silky that 
you won't run out of oil,

00:12:19.160 --> 00:12:22.700
and it has a rich flavor, like sesame oil.

00:12:22.700 --> 00:12:24.960
You're right on the money 
with that kind of thinking!

00:12:24.960 --> 00:12:25.770
Yep!

00:12:26.100 --> 00:12:27.770
So get cookin'!

00:12:27.770 --> 00:12:28.940
Matsu, get cooking!

00:12:28.940 --> 00:12:29.640
Right!

00:12:40.380 --> 00:12:41.380
Alright!

00:12:43.080 --> 00:12:47.720
We don't have any eggs, so I'll just 
have to fry them with flour and water.

00:12:50.120 --> 00:12:53.230
The fish and oil both have plenty of body,

00:12:53.230 --> 00:12:55.730
so they should come out 
tasty even without eggs.

00:12:57.560 --> 00:13:01.070
That's more like karaage or 
french-frying it than tempura.

00:13:01.070 --> 00:13:03.640
I'm surprised you carry around flour...

00:13:03.970 --> 00:13:07.670
I always have simple cooking 
ingredients and seasonings on me.

00:13:07.670 --> 00:13:08.710
Huh...

00:13:08.710 --> 00:13:12.040
And I just happen to have a 
great seasoning with me today...

00:13:12.040 --> 00:13:13.510
A great seasoning?

00:13:13.510 --> 00:13:15.250
Alright! I'm ready to fry.

00:13:19.350 --> 00:13:22.320
At first, the oil will splatter a lot because

00:13:22.320 --> 00:13:24.460
there's still water in the meat and bones,

00:13:24.460 --> 00:13:26.660
but I think it'll simmer 
down after a few minutes.

00:13:27.430 --> 00:13:29.890
It's still glowing, even though 
we're frying it in oil!

00:13:30.490 --> 00:13:32.660
It's overflowing with sparkling bubbles.

00:13:33.000 --> 00:13:35.070
Even though you're just frying it...

00:13:35.800 --> 00:13:38.270
What a divine sight!

00:13:38.270 --> 00:13:40.040
Yep, I think it's about done...

00:13:40.870 --> 00:13:42.340
Glowing tempura!

00:13:42.340 --> 00:13:43.670
Ye gods! What is this?!

00:13:43.670 --> 00:13:45.840
This is the first time I've 
seen anything like this!

00:13:46.080 --> 00:13:50.650
So aromatic! No matter what, 
I wanna eat it while it's hot!

00:13:50.650 --> 00:13:54.990
Alright, Komatsu! Fry up three 
apiece for us! I'm ready to eat!

00:13:54.990 --> 00:13:55.620
Right!

00:14:00.290 --> 00:14:02.630
Okay! The cooking's done!

00:14:02.630 --> 00:14:04.460
It's so beautiful!

00:14:04.460 --> 00:14:05.330
They sparkle!

00:14:05.330 --> 00:14:06.260
No, I mean the oil!

00:14:06.260 --> 00:14:08.000
This tempura looks delicious!

00:14:08.000 --> 00:14:10.070
It's the oil that's beautiful!

00:14:10.530 --> 00:14:11.330
The oil?

00:14:11.130 --> 00:14:14.000
The oil isn't dirty at all!

00:14:14.000 --> 00:14:16.170
I could understand if 
we just used vegetables,

00:14:16.170 --> 00:14:18.370
but we fried fish and it's still translucent.

00:14:18.370 --> 00:14:21.040
It looks like this oil can be used forever!

00:14:21.040 --> 00:14:25.480
That's incredible, Komatsu! You 
discovered a new natural cooking oil!

00:14:26.050 --> 00:14:28.980
I know! We got the oil 
from the Mors Mountains,

00:14:28.980 --> 00:14:30.550
so let's call it Mors Oil!

00:14:30.550 --> 00:14:34.820
Why do you get to name it?! And 
besides, "Mors Oil" is too simple.

00:14:34.820 --> 00:14:39.060
I think it's fine! Now come on, 
let's eat before the food gets cold!

00:14:39.060 --> 00:14:40.760
Oh, that's right!

00:14:40.760 --> 00:14:43.730
Okay, the food is ready. Now 
we just need the situation.

00:14:44.300 --> 00:14:45.500
Situa...

00:14:44.730 --> 00:14:45.500
Queen!

00:14:51.870 --> 00:14:55.080
Now, Queen! Stretch out this 
stretchy body of yours!

00:15:09.090 --> 00:15:10.990
How high are we?!

00:15:12.060 --> 00:15:15.660
The muscle it must take to 
stand vertically like this...

00:15:15.660 --> 00:15:18.830
Well, right now, we're only 
about 800 meters high.

00:15:18.830 --> 00:15:20.270
800 meters?!

00:15:20.270 --> 00:15:23.670
But even so, it's a marvelous 
view for having a meal!

00:15:26.210 --> 00:15:28.380
Well, let's eat!

00:15:28.380 --> 00:15:32.810
I give thanks for all of this world's 
great bounty... Shining Gourami!

00:15:32.810 --> 00:15:34.480
Thank you!

00:15:36.050 --> 00:15:39.890
It's like a fish made from solid gold!

00:15:46.890 --> 00:15:48.900
The outside is deliciously 
browned and crispy.

00:15:48.900 --> 00:15:52.130
It's like a lightly coated rice 
cracker with several layers.

00:15:52.130 --> 00:15:54.600
And I don't detect any bones.

00:15:54.600 --> 00:15:57.470
The inside is moist, succulent, juicy!

00:15:57.470 --> 00:16:02.340
The rich flavor slowly 
flows from the tender meat!

00:16:02.880 --> 00:16:05.340
My body is brimming with power!

00:16:05.340 --> 00:16:08.850
D-Delicious!

00:16:09.510 --> 00:16:12.950
The meat is silver! I've never 
seen meat like this before!

00:16:12.950 --> 00:16:15.390
This ingredient is too beautiful!

00:16:15.390 --> 00:16:20.330
Still, with this beauty, I was so 
sure my cell level would increase,

00:16:20.690 --> 00:16:22.560
but is something missing?

00:16:22.560 --> 00:16:25.930
I have indeed regained my strength, 
and yet not to the max...

00:16:25.930 --> 00:16:28.130
The flavor is strong and rich,

00:16:28.130 --> 00:16:31.440
but it leaves a bland 
taste and texture behind.

00:16:31.740 --> 00:16:33.670
I think I know what would go well with it.

00:16:33.670 --> 00:16:35.410
That seasoning...

00:16:35.410 --> 00:16:37.010
You mean...

00:16:37.710 --> 00:16:41.250
That's right! Let's give 
it a try. Melk Stardust!

00:16:41.250 --> 00:16:42.550
Melk Stardust?!

00:16:42.550 --> 00:16:45.720
I thought I smelled something 
good coming from your backpack!

00:16:45.720 --> 00:16:48.290
So you brought along Melk Stardust, huh?!

00:16:48.290 --> 00:16:49.150
Uh-huh!

00:16:49.590 --> 00:16:52.620
I used it as markers in the cavern.

00:16:52.620 --> 00:16:55.890
Of course, I retrieved all 
of it on the way back...

00:16:55.690 --> 00:17:00.560
I was wondering how that tastes, 
since you guys wouldn't tell me!

00:17:00.560 --> 00:17:03.370
There's a reason we didn't tell you.

00:17:03.370 --> 00:17:04.270
A reason?

00:17:04.270 --> 00:17:07.640
Melk Stardust is very addictive.

00:17:07.640 --> 00:17:09.310
Don't tell me it's a narcotic ingredient...

00:17:09.310 --> 00:17:11.240
No, it's not like that.

00:17:11.040 --> 00:17:13.140
Anyway, it's too delicious.

00:17:14.340 --> 00:17:18.380
It's composed of a new kind of amino acid 
with an overwhelmingly savory flavor.

00:17:18.380 --> 00:17:21.580
Thanks to that, it's like a magic spice 
that attacks your appetite directly.

00:17:21.580 --> 00:17:24.250
Once you try it, you don't 
want to stop eating it.

00:17:24.620 --> 00:17:26.090
This is it!

00:17:26.520 --> 00:17:27.720
Beautiful!

00:17:28.120 --> 00:17:29.590
The first time we ate it,

00:17:29.590 --> 00:17:33.260
Melk-san and I were so hooked 
that we couldn't stop licking it!

00:17:33.260 --> 00:17:36.100
The problem is that no matter how 
much you sprinkle on an ingredient,

00:17:36.100 --> 00:17:38.770
it dominates the ingredient.

00:17:38.770 --> 00:17:40.800
So it's no good with your average ingredient.

00:17:40.800 --> 00:17:43.970
It has to be used with an ingredient that's 
got the impact of, say, Jewel Meat.

00:17:43.970 --> 00:17:45.810
Like Shining Gourami?

00:17:45.810 --> 00:17:47.940
Yes! That might not lose 
to the Stardust's flavor.

00:17:47.940 --> 00:17:49.710
They may work together in harmony...

00:17:49.980 --> 00:17:51.350
It's worth a try!

00:17:51.680 --> 00:17:52.310
Right!

00:17:54.150 --> 00:17:56.790
Gold spice on silver meat...

00:17:56.790 --> 00:17:58.820
This meeting of ingredients is art!

00:18:02.590 --> 00:18:05.360
There's no doubt about it! 
This harmony between them,

00:18:05.360 --> 00:18:07.560
it's a fateful encounter!

00:18:16.140 --> 00:18:20.140
This is what I'm talking 
about! An exact match!

00:18:20.140 --> 00:18:24.480
Like a missing puzzle piece, 
it fits my body perfectly!

00:18:24.480 --> 00:18:27.550
I can feel power flooding 
my tank all at once!

00:18:35.920 --> 00:18:36.920
Toriko...

00:18:41.390 --> 00:18:43.160
Gross!

00:18:43.160 --> 00:18:45.230
I was right...

00:18:45.800 --> 00:18:48.230
It's delicious...

00:18:51.770 --> 00:18:53.110
Death Falls...

00:18:53.410 --> 00:18:55.410
If the three of us hadn't 
combined our efforts,

00:18:55.410 --> 00:18:57.980
we wouldn't have been able to 
capture the Shining Gourami.

00:18:57.780 --> 00:19:01.780
I'm sure the Gourmet World has even 
more disgusting raging waterfalls.

00:19:01.780 --> 00:19:03.280
We'd better build up more strength.

00:19:03.280 --> 00:19:06.620
Queen-chan played a huge 
part this time around, too.

00:19:09.290 --> 00:19:12.830
I hope that one day, Coco-san 
and Zebra-san can join us, too,

00:19:12.830 --> 00:19:16.160
and we can all go on a trip together...

00:19:16.830 --> 00:19:18.360
That would be the best...

00:19:18.360 --> 00:19:20.130
No thanks! It'd be annoying!

00:19:20.770 --> 00:19:22.800
Zebra is disgusting, and Coco...

00:19:22.800 --> 00:19:24.500
He's not disgusting!

00:19:24.500 --> 00:19:27.070
Yeah, he's quick to anger when he thinks 
you're being cocky and that's scary...

00:19:27.070 --> 00:19:28.540
That's what I mean by annoying!

00:19:28.540 --> 00:19:31.340
But he's really dependable! Coco, too...

00:19:31.340 --> 00:19:33.180
Coco's gross, too, because he's poisonous!

00:19:33.180 --> 00:19:34.580
He's not gross!

00:19:33.550 --> 00:19:34.750
Komatsu...

00:19:34.080 --> 00:19:35.650
Did you know this, Sunny-san?

00:19:35.280 --> 00:19:36.680
Hmm...

00:19:35.650 --> 00:19:38.780
The person who says, "Gross! 
Gross!" is the one that's gross.

00:19:37.180 --> 00:19:41.690
Just like the old days, it'd be nice 
to travel with Sunny, Coco, and Zebra.

00:19:42.350 --> 00:19:46.720
And more than anything, we need you, Komatsu.

00:19:46.720 --> 00:19:48.460
Toriko-san? What's wrong?

00:19:49.090 --> 00:19:50.260
Nothing...

00:19:52.100 --> 00:19:55.630
Come on, Komatsu! Keep fryin' 
those Shining Gourami!

00:19:55.630 --> 00:19:56.300
Right!

00:19:58.070 --> 00:20:01.440
You want some too, Queen? 
Alright, fry up all the rest!

00:20:01.440 --> 00:20:04.040
All the rest? There's not that much left...

00:20:04.040 --> 00:20:06.540
What are you talking about?! Just fry!

00:20:06.540 --> 00:20:07.740
Um...

00:20:08.980 --> 00:20:10.080
Hurry up!

00:20:15.750 --> 00:20:19.620
They repelled a 5,000-meter tall mountain...

00:20:32.800 --> 00:20:35.940
What a fine team they make.

00:21:39.830 --> 00:21:42.000
This week's Gourmet Fortune!

00:21:43.040 --> 00:21:45.940
It's time for Gourmet Fortune, with 
a heaping helping of accuracy!

00:21:46.740 --> 00:21:50.380
We're going to use a camera this 
time too, so get yours ready!

00:21:50.640 --> 00:21:53.580
Okay, please choose one 
of these three platters.

00:21:54.210 --> 00:21:58.180
This week's lucky ingredient 
is in one of them!

00:21:59.150 --> 00:22:02.020
The higher the capture level, 
the more Gourmet Luck it has!

00:22:02.960 --> 00:22:05.090
Alright, here we go!

00:22:05.090 --> 00:22:06.630
A heaping helping...

00:22:07.490 --> 00:22:09.200
Open!

00:22:11.260 --> 00:22:13.730
This week's best Gourmet Luck is...

00:22:14.570 --> 00:22:19.640
A - Salamander Sphinx Capture Level 92

00:22:14.900 --> 00:22:16.670
...yours if you chose A!

00:22:16.670 --> 00:22:19.540
I have a hunch you're going to get 
close fast with that girl you like.

00:22:19.640 --> 00:22:25.980
C - Mystery Bird Rubanda Capture Level 30

00:22:20.040 --> 00:22:23.240
If you chose C, you get this 
week's second-best luck.

00:22:23.240 --> 00:22:25.980
You may just find that item you've 
been looking the longest time for!

00:22:25.980 --> 00:22:31.720
B - Striped Salmon Capture Level <1

00:22:26.280 --> 00:22:29.480
And I'm sorry. If you chose B, you're third.

00:22:29.480 --> 00:22:31.720
Don't take anything on so easily.

00:22:31.950 --> 00:22:35.220
And finally, it's Gourmet 
Good Luck Charm photo time!

00:22:35.220 --> 00:22:36.720
Are you ready?

00:22:36.460 --> 00:22:42.360
Good Luck Charm Photo Time

00:22:36.720 --> 00:22:38.920
If you take a photo of the scene,

00:22:38.920 --> 00:22:42.360
and carry it with you for a week as a 
good luck charm, you'll be even luckier!

00:22:42.590 --> 00:22:44.400
Alright, here we go!

00:22:44.400 --> 00:22:45.230
Three!

00:22:45.230 --> 00:22:46.130
Two!

00:22:46.130 --> 00:22:46.700
One!

00:22:46.700 --> 00:22:48.500
Scoop chance!

00:22:49.200 --> 00:22:51.500
Be prepared for anything!

00:22:51.500 --> 00:22:53.810
Preparation is everything!

00:22:54.110 --> 00:22:57.180
And that doesn't just apply to cooking.

00:22:57.180 --> 00:22:58.510
This has been Komatsu.

00:22:59.280 --> 00:23:02.750
Alright! Are you mentally 
prepared for the next segment?

00:23:02.750 --> 00:23:04.450
Then eagerly check it out!

00:23:07.080 --> 00:23:09.220
It's the opening of the Gourmet Service Tournament.

00:23:09.480 --> 00:23:12.960
Time to serve your guests with unprecedented impact!

00:23:13.560 --> 00:23:16.630
Flashy Presentation! Supreme Service With a Meal!

00:23:17.100 --> 00:23:18.940
Look forward to another heaping helping of fun!
